  "text": "Making classic Neapolitan ice cream is a delightful way to enjoy a traditional Italian treat. Neapolitan ice cream is a three-scoop combination of **vanilla**, **strawberry**, and **chocolate**. Here's a simple and delicious recipe you can follow at home.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf68 **Classic Neapolitan Ice Cream Recipe**\n\n#### \ud83c\udf53 **Ingredients** (for 6 servings):\n\n**Vanilla Ice Cream Base:**\n- 2 cups heavy cream\n- 1 cup whole milk\n- 3/4 cup sugar\n- 1 tablespoon vanilla extract\n- 1/4 teaspoon salt\n\n**Strawberry Ice Cream Base:**\n- 1 cup fresh strawberries (or 1/2 cup strawberry puree)\n- 1/2 cup sugar\n- 1 tablespoon cornstarch\n- 1/4 teaspoon salt\n- 1 cup heavy cream\n- 1 cup whole milk\n- 1 teaspoon vanilla extract\n\n**Chocolate Ice Cream Base:**\n- 2 cups heavy cream\n- 1 cup whole milk\n- 3/4 cup sugar\n- 1/2 cup unsweetened cocoa powder\n- 1/4 teaspoon salt\n- 2 tablespoons butter (optional, for richer taste)\n- 1 teaspoon vanilla extract\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd04 **Instructions**\n\n#### 1. **Make the Vanilla Base:**\n- In a saucepan, combine the heavy cream, milk, sugar, salt, and vanilla extract.\n- Heat over medium heat, stirring until the sugar dissolves.\n- Pour the mixture into an ice bath (a bowl of ice and water) and stir until it cools to about 40\u00b0F (4\u00b0C).\n- Churn in an ice cream maker according to the manufacturer\u2019s instructions until it reaches a soft-serve consistency.\n- Freeze for at least 2 hours to firm up.\n\n#### 2. **Make the Strawberry Base:**\n- In a saucepan, combine strawberries, sugar, cornstarch, and salt.\n- Cook over medium heat, stirring until the mixture thickens and the strawberries break down (about 5 minutes).\n- Let cool to room temperature.\n- In a separate bowl, mix heavy cream and milk, then gradually add the strawberry mixture. Stir well.\n- Churn in an ice cream maker until soft-serve consistency is reached, then freeze for at least 2 hours.\n\n#### 3. **Make the Chocolate Base:**\n- In a saucepan, combine heavy cream, milk, sugar, cocoa powder, salt, and butter (if using).\n- Heat over medium heat, stirring until the sugar dissolves and the mixture is smooth.\n- Pour into an ice bath and cool to about 40\u00b0F (4\u00b0C).\n- Churn in an ice cream maker until soft-serve consistency, then freeze for at least 2 hours.\n\n#### 4. **Assemble Neapolitan Ice Cream:**\n- Scoop 1/3 vanilla, 1/3 strawberry, and 1/3 chocolate ice cream into a serving bowl.\n- Serve immediately or chill before serving for a firmer texture.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf70 **Tips:**\n- Use an ice cream maker for best results, though you can make it by hand by stirring frequently and freezing in a bowl with ice and salt.\n- For a richer chocolate flavor, use high-quality cocoa or chocolate chips.\n- Always store in the freezer and consume within 1\u20132 weeks for best taste.\n\nEnjoy your homemade classic Neapolitan ice cream! \ud83c\udf66",
